// The SQL engine's Count and Reindex are the engine's own: a double of the
// port has no tables to count or to file again.
//
// Consistency: a call reads at the isolation of the transaction it runs on. A
// write is visible to its own transaction at once, and to every other one
// once it commits — never before, and never if it rolls back; a REPEATABLE
// READ caller reads its own snapshot. A call on the pool is its own
// transaction, and reads what is committed.
